CommitDate: Thu Sep 24 23:06:54 2026 -0500

    fix: AUG-062 confidence sentinel -1.0 no longer leaks into user-facing output
    
    `answer` without --confidence stores the spec'd -1 sentinel ("asserted directly,
    not scored by a model") — that stays in the store unchanged — but it leaked into
    every reader: dump and the answer echo printed a bare -1.0, feedback's
    `0 <= c < 0.60` filter read the unmeasured decision as CONFIDENT (reporting
    "every recorded decision is at or above the threshold" while one had never been
    scored), and the priority-judgment branch escalated it as "-1.00 below the 0.30
    floor". Fix shape: one renderer (_conf_render — n/a for the sentinel) now serves
    every user-facing confidence render (answer echo, dump header, feedback thin
    list + proposer state + opens-edge note, ask seats state, status drill list);
    aggregations go through _conf_values, so status min/mean/max and the
    coverage-by-domain means exclude the sentinel; thin_decisions treats unmeasured
    as thin alongside the measured-thin band. Ordering chosen for thin_decisions:
    measured rows by confidence then id, then unmeasured rows by id. Priority-
    judgment choice: SKIP numeric escalation for unmeasured rows — the 0.30 floor is
    a judgment about a measurement, and an unmeasured decision never failed one; it
    is still drilled like any other thin decision. Sites left rendering raw on
    purpose (model-stated values that can never hold the decision sentinel): ask's
    completeness/subject/question echoes, the impact-verdict refusal line, and
    verdict --list's dash for a scoreless (never-sentinel) verdict. The stale
    thin_decisions docstring ("unknown is not low") now states the new behavior.
    
    RED (pre-fix): AssertionError: D-001 recorded  (confidence -1.0, 1 of 2 active, embedded, scope project)
    GREEN (post-fix): 177 passed (172 prior + 5 new AUG-062 tests) in 570s; ruff check auger.py clean; gate tail: "GATE PASS"
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
